A||||7||SteveJ||It rains on my engine !||||1||
Z||000000||SteveJ||02-14-2001||11:36 AM||||So the '84 is the only one with louvers over the engine. In the last 3-4 inches closest to the window it doesn't have 2 levels of louvers like the forward part does. Am I missing a part that shunts the rain off the engine?<BR>I was driving home recently when there was an explosion in the rear and the engine started to miss badly. Buy driving one foot on the gas and using the other to brake I got it home. It had blown the porcelain part of the plug right out. The steel retaining it in had rusted right out. AC plugs - been in there about a year. (creative use of large screw extractor required) I gotta blame the rain that collects in the plug recess.<BR>Am I missing a baffle ?||||reg||1
Z||000001||KRMFiero||02-14-2001||12:42 PM||||When it rains out and stuff my Valve Cover and everything closer to the firewall gets wet<BR>Does that help?<P><BR>Kyle||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||02-14-2001||01:15 PM||||They weren't Champion plugs? (inside joke)<P>Best advise I can give is to put a skim coat of grease on the metal and threads to help keep the rust from eating that rolled edge away and keep the plugs from siezing to the block.<P>I think there was a tray under the vents but It was removed as part of the recall items.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TheFiero64||02-14-2001||04:02 PM||||Yep. All 84's get a free engine wash whenever it rains out.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
