Z||000007||daved||02-14-2001||09:28 PM||||I made a new seal to replace the one removed by the recall.  I think it was thought to be a fire hazard, so GM took it off.  It really keeps the rain out of the plug recesses, though you have to realise if you open a wet trunk lid, the water still runs down over the damn engine!<BR>I fabricated an aluminum strip (from J strip aluminum siding, though anything at hand will do).  I used the rubber door seal from a Ford pickup! 'cause I had it. Drilled holes to suit the little plastic push-in xmas tree clips, and attached the assembly to the the rear lip of the trunk.  It fits tight against the glass when the trunk is closed. Now my engine doesnt miss in the rain any more.  Dave||||reg||1
